  <data name="InfoTipName" xml:space="preserve"><value>Help</value></data>
  <data name="UserNameTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Up to 20 characters; spaces inside are fine.
Not allowed: &quot; / \ [ ] : ; | = , + * ? &lt; &gt; @ % and built-in account names (Administrator, Guest).
Examples: Anna, Alex, Ivan Petrov.</value></data>
  <data name="PasswordModeTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>&quot;Set at first sign-in&quot; — the account is created without a password, and Windows asks for a new one right at the first sign-in. The image holds no password.
&quot;Store in the image&quot; — the password goes into the answer file, and anyone with this ISO can read it. Needed for automatic sign-in and hands-off installs.</value></data>
  <data name="ComputerNameTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Up to 15 characters: Latin letters, digits and hyphens; not digits only.
Examples: HOME-PC, OFFICE-01, LAPTOP.
Empty — Windows picks a name like DESKTOP-ABC1234.</value></data>
  <data name="RegionalTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Formats — how dates, times, numbers and currency look (US: 12/31/2026, 1,234.5).
Keyboards — input languages, switched with Win+Space.
Time zone — the clock.
None of this changes the Windows display language: English Windows with Russian formats and keyboard is fine.</value></data>
  <data name="KeyboardsTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The first keyboard is the main one: Windows starts with it, and the sign-in password is typed with it.
Example: English (US) first and Russian second — the password in Latin letters, switch with Win+Space.</value></data>
  <data name="ProductKeyTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>A 25-character key: XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX — from the sticker, the purchase email or your Microsoft account.
Not needed if this computer already had activated Windows of the same edition: the license is tied to the hardware, and Windows activates itself once online.
Shapeshift activates nothing and contains no keys.</value></data>
  <data name="InstallEditionTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>&quot;Ask during setup&quot; — the installer shows the list of editions as usual.
A specific edition — installed without asking. Pick the one you have a license for: usually Pro or Home (store-bought laptops mostly come with Home).</value></data>
  <data name="WorkspaceTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Needs a local drive with about 2–3 times the ISO size free. Not a USB stick or a network folder.
A good example: D:\Shapeshift. Long paths like C:\Users\Name\Documents\Projects\Images may not fit in the Windows path length limit.</value></data>
  <data name="AppsTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Removing takes the app out of the image: new users won&apos;t get it. It can be reinstalled from Microsoft Store.
No mark — safe to remove. &quot;Recommended&quot; checks ad-driven and rarely needed apps.
The ⚠ icon — other parts of Windows depend on the app (Store, Windows Security, codecs, winget). Those are shown only in advanced mode.</value></data>
  <data name="ProgramsTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Checkboxes and the id box — programs from winget: downloaded at the first sign-in, so the internet is needed.
&quot;Add installer…&quot; — your own .exe, .msi, .cmd, .bat or .ps1: copied into the image and installed offline.
&quot;Add installer folder…&quot; — a multi-file distribution such as Office.
Installed in order; one failing program doesn&apos;t stop the rest.</value></data>
  <data name="WingetIdTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The id is the exact package name in the winget catalog, like Publisher.Program.
Find it: run winget search telegram in a terminal and take the &quot;Id&quot; column, or look it up on winstall.app.
Examples: Telegram.TelegramDesktop, Mozilla.Thunderbird, 7zip.7zip.</value></data>
  <data name="AddInstallerTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Use a folder when the installer needs files next to it.
Office: the folder with setup.exe from the Office Deployment Tool and configuration.xml; run setup.exe with /configure configuration.xml (Office downloads at the first sign-in unless configuration.xml points to a local source).</value></data>
  <data name="ProgramArgsTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Options that make the installer ask nothing. They depend on what built the installer:
• Inno Setup: /VERYSILENT /NORESTART
• NSIS: /S
• InstallShield: /s /v&quot;/qn&quot;
• .msi: nothing — /qn /norestart are added automatically; properties like ALLUSERS=1 are fine
• Office (ODT): /configure configuration.xml
To find out: setup.exe /? or the program&apos;s download page.</value></data>
