  <data name="UupInsiderBar.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>This is a preview version of Windows: it may be unstable, and tweaks may not work.</value></data>
  <data name="UupLanguageBox.Header" xml:space="preserve"><value>Windows language</value></data>
  <data name="UupLanguageTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The display language Windows is installed with.
Date formats, keyboards and the time zone are set separately, on the Setup step.</value></data>
  <data name="UupEditionsHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Editions</value></data>
  <data name="UupEditionsTip.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>These are the editions Microsoft publishes ready-made: Home and Pro (and their N versions without media features, for Europe).
Education, Enterprise, Pro for Workstations and others are made from Pro and will come later.
Pick the one you have a license for.</value></data>
  <data name="UupNotYetBar.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>What you get</value></data>
  <data name="UupNotYetBar.Message" xml:space="preserve"><value>From here it works as with your own ISO: the image is built from Windows Update files, with the latest update if it is checked. Such an image has no built-in apps (Store, Photos and so on) yet; they come in later versions of Shapeshift. You can download the files in advance, or the build downloads them itself.</value></data>
